# bento.page response headers (Cloudflare Workers static assets).
# They reproduce what the site served on GitHub Pages. Shipped decks opened
# from file:// fetch the release channel cross-origin, so
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin is load-bearing: never remove it. Security
# headers come later, deliberately, not as a side effect of a host move.
#
# How Workers applies this file (read in wrangler 4.152.0's asset worker):
# rules run in file order; the FIRST rule to set a
# header replaces the asset's own value, a later matching rule APPENDS with a
# comma, and "! Name" deletes. A path written twice keeps only its last block.
# So every header is set under /* only, and a rule that needs a different
# Content-Type deletes the /* one first.
#
# Content-Type is set here, not left to the platform: GitHub Pages sent
# "; charset=utf-8" on every text type, production Workers sends none (local
# wrangler dev does, so an emulator run cannot show the difference). /* covers
# every HTML page, the rewritten forms (/, /d/, /x) and every 404, whose body
# is always 404.html. Everything below the generated marker is written by
# scripts/site-routing.mjs from the published tree: one rule per file that is
# not HTML, and one per directory 301, whose empty body keeps no type.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: max-age=600
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

# ---- generated by scripts/site-routing.mjs; do not edit below ----
